WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.678
Not every learning asset belongs only inside the course player.

00:00:03.678 --> 00:00:07.614
Job aids, checklists, worksheets, quick reference guides, policy summaries, lab guides,

00:00:07.614 --> 00:00:11.550
and printable handouts can support learners after the course is complete.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:16.559
These resources are especially valuable when the real task happens later, under time pressure,

00:00:16.559 --> 00:00:18.706
or away from the training environment.

00:00:18.706 --> 00:00:20.495
Tools such as InDesign, Acrobat,

00:00:20.495 --> 00:00:25.147
or similar document-production tools can support polished downloadable resources at a high level.

00:00:25.147 --> 00:00:26.936
The design should prioritize usability.

00:00:26.936 --> 00:00:31.588
A job aid should be easy to scan, easy to print when needed,

00:00:31.588 --> 00:00:33.019
and easy to update.

00:00:33.019 --> 00:00:38.028
It should not be a decorative brochure if the learner needs a working reference.

00:00:38.028 --> 00:00:39.459
Accessible document design matters.

00:00:39.459 --> 00:00:42.680
Use meaningful headings, readable text, logical structure, sufficient contrast,

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.900
descriptive links, and alternative text planning for meaningful images.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.689
If a PDF is distributed,

00:00:47.689 --> 00:00:53.414
the team should consider whether it can be navigated and understood by learners using assistive technology.

00:00:53.414 --> 00:00:56.992
Accessibility is part of the asset, not an optional afterthought.

00:00:56.992 --> 00:01:00.928
Versioning is important for downloadable resources because learners may save copies.

00:01:00.928 --> 00:01:04.148
Include a clear title, date or version where appropriate,

00:01:04.148 --> 00:01:07.011
and ownership information if the organization uses it.

00:01:07.011 --> 00:01:11.305
Keep source files and export files organized so updates can be made

00:01:11.305 --> 00:01:13.809
without rebuilding the entire course from scratch.

00:01:13.809 --> 00:01:16.314
Align job aids with real workplace tasks.

00:01:16.314 --> 00:01:19.177
A good checklist supports a decision or action.

00:01:19.177 --> 00:01:21.681
A worksheet helps learners apply a process.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:25.975
A quick reference guide helps them remember steps without replaying a module.

00:01:25.975 --> 00:01:31.700
Downloadable resources are most valuable when they extend the course into the learner actual work environment.
